{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["Let us deal wisely with him — so that he does not multiply, for if he multiplies and it happens that war befalls [us] from our enemies — as in: ידה ליתד תשלחנה — we find singular form used for plural." "When it befalls — when it occurs, as in: מקראי קודש מארע קודשא — the language of occurrence." "And fight against us and go up from the land — to return to the land of their fathers. And it is not good for us to lose our slaves; and they call it מלכותא קטיעא ['a maimed kingdom']."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "Rashbam reads the suffix -לו 'with him' as singular for the collective Israel; the lemma and syntax suggest the plan aims to prevent Israel from multiplying."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:40:08.911828633Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}